.agents/
BUILD-BRIEF.md
WAVEB-SOULS.json

artifacts/isola/.next/
artifacts/isola/.next-preview/

# --- repository contamination (added 2026-07-31 after the Replit Agent incident) ---
# A git bundle is a whole repository inside this one; it does not belong in the
# tree. evidence/stage1/isola-stage1.bundle is already TRACKED, so this rule
# does not affect it — gitignore only governs untracked files.
*.bundle
# A timestamped copy of the Prisma schema forks the schema next to the
# canonical file, where a later edit can land on the wrong one. The canonical
# schema.prisma and everything under prisma/migrations/ are unaffected.
schema.prisma.backup.*

# --- governed engineering environment (added 2026-08-05, first source-controlled bootstrap) ---
# TRACKED, deliberately: .claude/settings.json and .claude/hooks/** — the reusable,
# machine-independent enforcement layer.
#
# tools/claude-plugins/ (a packaged mirror of the above, generated by package-plugin.js
# for optional installation as a Claude Code plugin) was removed 2026-09-05
# (dec-c360-ops-procedure-registry-2026-09-05): it was never installed anywhere, had
# zero references outside its own generator, and no CI ever wired its own --check mode
# — a second copy with no enforcement and no consumer, not a reusable artifact. Plugins
# in this platform must be self-contained copies (they cannot require() files outside
# their own directory once installed), so there is no "load, not copy" fix available —
# if this pack is ever needed as an installable plugin again, regenerate it fresh from
# .claude/ rather than resurrecting a stale copy.
#
# Everything listed below is per-machine runtime state, a local override, or generated
# evidence. None of it is reproducible across machines and none of it may enter the
# repository. Rules are per-path rather than a blanket `.claude/` so that adding a new
# tracked hook never requires a negation rule.
.claude/state/
.claude/memo-evidence/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/**/*.log
# Credential / OAuth material the CLI may write next to project settings.
.claude/.credentials.json
.claude/oauth*.json
